 ("p", "Until the middle of the twentieth century production was largely organised within countries. What crossed boundaries were raw materials, food stuff and finished products; colonies such as India exported raw materials and imported finished goods. Trade was the main channel connecting distant countries. This changed when large companies called **multinational corporations (MNCs)** emerged."),
